IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `aia-core`
IMPORT `aia-timeline`
IMPORT `aia-scope`
IMPORT `P2-section-2-gate`

-- P2-art-9: Article 9 (risk management system) of the EU Artificial Intelligence Act, Regulation (EU) 2024/1689 as amended by Regulation (EU) 2026/1744.
-- The Omnibus did not change Article 9. Every function takes the date asked, the AI system and the harmonisation facts and answers through the gate of P2-section-2-gate.l4:
-- NOTHING when Chapter III Sections 1 to 3 do not apply to the system on the date asked, JUST FALSE where Article 2(2) cuts the Article off, NOTHING where Article 2(13) says it may be limited.
-- Reading a result: JUST TRUE the text's requirement is met on the facts; JUST FALSE the text says no (a flat "shall" not done); NOTHING not covered.
-- Open-textured judgments ("appropriate", "acceptable", "as far as technically feasible") are plain yes/no inputs; a limb the text qualifies with "where appropriate" is answered yes where it is not appropriate.

§ `Article 9(1): a risk management system`

-- src:270 | 1. A risk management system shall be established, implemented, documented and maintained in relation to high-risk AI systems.
@ref Art 9(1) (src:270)
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
      `the AI system` IS AN `AI system`
      `the harmonisation facts` IS A `Arts 8 to 15 harmonisation facts`
      `a risk management system has been established in relation to the high-risk AI system` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the risk management system has been implemented` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the risk management system has been documented` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the risk management system has been maintained` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 9(1) a risk management system has been established, implemented, documented and maintained in relation to the high-risk AI system` MEANS
    CONSIDER `Arts 8 to 15 the gate for the requirement` `the date asked` `the AI system` `the harmonisation facts` (`Article reference` OF 9, "", 1)
    WHEN `Arts 8 to 15 gate the requirement applies` THEN
        JUST (`a risk management system has been established in relation to the high-risk AI system` AND `the risk management system has been implemented` AND `the risk management system has been documented` AND `the risk management system has been maintained`)  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A risk management system shall be established, implemented, documented and maintained in relation to high-risk AI systems"
    WHEN `Arts 8 to 15 gate cut off by Article 2(2)` THEN JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): Article 2(2) "only Article 6(1), Article 60a and Articles 102 to 112 shall apply" to a high-risk AI system under Article 6(1) related to Section B products (seam S14, the keel's answer)
    WHEN `Arts 8 to 15 gate may be limited under Article 2(13)` THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): Article 2(13) says the application of this requirement "may be limited"; how far is for the delegated acts it names
    OTHERWISE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): Chapter III Section 2 applies from the date Article 113(c) gives, and Article 111(2) saves a system placed earlier and not significantly changed


§ `Article 9(2): the process and its steps`

-- src:271 | 2. The risk management system shall be understood as a continuous iterative process planned and run throughout the entire lifecycle of a high-risk AI system, requiring regular systematic review and updating. It shall comprise the following steps:
-- src:272 | (a) the identification and analysis of the known and the reasonably foreseeable risks that the high-risk AI system can pose to health, safety or fundamental rights when the high-risk AI system is used in accordance with its intended purpose;
-- src:273 | (b) the estimation and evaluation of the risks that may emerge when the high-risk AI system is used in accordance with its intended purpose, and under conditions of reasonably foreseeable misuse;
-- src:274 | (c) the evaluation of other risks possibly arising, based on the analysis of data gathered from the post-market monitoring system referred to in Article 72;
-- src:275 | (d) the adoption of appropriate and targeted risk management measures designed to address the risks identified pursuant to point (a).
@ref Art 9(2) (src:271-275)
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
      `the AI system` IS AN `AI system`
      `the harmonisation facts` IS A `Arts 8 to 15 harmonisation facts`
      `the risk management system is a continuous iterative process planned and run throughout the entire lifecycle of the high-risk AI system` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the process involves regular systematic review and updating` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the process comprises the identification and analysis of the known and the reasonably foreseeable risks that the high-risk AI system can pose to health, safety or fundamental rights when it is used in accordance with its intended purpose` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the process comprises the estimation and evaluation of the risks that may emerge when the high-risk AI system is used in accordance with its intended purpose, and under conditions of reasonably foreseeable misuse` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the process comprises the evaluation of other risks possibly arising, based on the analysis of data gathered from the post-market monitoring system referred to in Article 72` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the process comprises the adoption of appropriate and targeted risk management measures designed to address the risks identified pursuant to point (a)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 9(2) the risk management system is a continuous iterative process comprising the following steps` MEANS
    CONSIDER `Arts 8 to 15 the gate for the requirement` `the date asked` `the AI system` `the harmonisation facts` (`Article reference` OF 9, "", 2)
    WHEN `Arts 8 to 15 gate the requirement applies` THEN
        JUST (`the risk management system is a continuous iterative process planned and run throughout the entire lifecycle of the high-risk AI system` AND `the process involves regular systematic review and updating` AND `the process comprises the identification and analysis of the known and the reasonably foreseeable risks that the high-risk AI system can pose to health, safety or fundamental rights when it is used in accordance with its intended purpose` AND `the process comprises the estimation and evaluation of the risks that may emerge when the high-risk AI system is used in accordance with its intended purpose, and under conditions of reasonably foreseeable misuse` AND `the process comprises the evaluation of other risks possibly arising, based on the analysis of data gathered from the post-market monitoring system referred to in Article 72` AND `the process comprises the adoption of appropriate and targeted risk management measures designed to address the risks identified pursuant to point (a)`)  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "shall be understood as a continuous iterative process ... It shall comprise the following steps"
    WHEN `Arts 8 to 15 gate cut off by Article 2(2)` THEN JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): Article 2(2) "only Article 6(1), Article 60a and Articles 102 to 112 shall apply" to a high-risk AI system under Article 6(1) related to Section B products (seam S14, the keel's answer)
    WHEN `Arts 8 to 15 gate may be limited under Article 2(13)` THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): Article 2(13) says the application of this requirement "may be limited"; how far is for the delegated acts it names
    OTHERWISE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): Chapter III Section 2 applies from the date Article 113(c) gives, and Article 111(2) saves a system placed earlier and not significantly changed


