§ `Article 9(7): testing in real-world conditions`

-- src:285 | 7. Testing procedures may include testing in real-world conditions in accordance with Article 60.
@ref Art 9(7) (src:285)
-- A liberty ("may include"). Seam S7: the fact that all the conditions of Article 60 are fulfilled is P7's answer, taken here as a plain input.
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
      `the AI system` IS AN `AI system`
      `the harmonisation facts` IS A `Arts 8 to 15 harmonisation facts`
      `all the conditions laid down in Article 60 for testing in real-world conditions are fulfilled` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 9(7) testing procedures may include testing in real-world conditions in accordance with Article 60` MEANS
    CONSIDER `Arts 8 to 15 the gate for the requirement` `the date asked` `the AI system` `the harmonisation facts` (`Article reference` OF 9, "", 7)
    WHEN `Arts 8 to 15 gate the requirement applies` THEN
        IF NOT (`all the conditions laid down in Article 60 for testing in real-world conditions are fulfilled`)
        THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): "may include testing in real-world conditions in accordance with Article 60": the sentence names this option and says nothing of any other
