    WHEN `Arts 8 to 15 gate cut off by Article 2(2)` THEN JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): Article 2(2) "only Article 6(1), Article 60a and Articles 102 to 112 shall apply" to a high-risk AI system under Article 6(1) related to Section B products (seam S14, the keel's answer)
    WHEN `Arts 8 to 15 gate may be limited under Article 2(13)` THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): Article 2(13) says the application of this requirement "may be limited"; how far is for the delegated acts it names
    OTHERWISE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): Chapter III Section 2 applies from the date Article 113(c) gives, and Article 111(2) saves a system placed earlier and not significantly changed


§ `Article 9(8): when and against what the testing is performed`

-- src:286 | The testing of high-risk AI systems shall be performed, as appropriate, at any time throughout the development process, and, in any event, prior to their being placed on the market or put into service.
@ref Art 9(8) first sentence (src:286)
-- "in any event, prior to their being placed on the market or put into service": the testing date must fall before the date the system was placed on the market or put into service (the core's AI system record).
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
      `the AI system` IS AN `AI system`
      `the harmonisation facts` IS A `Arts 8 to 15 harmonisation facts`
      `the testing is performed, as appropriate, at any time throughout the development process` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the date on which the testing of the high-risk AI system was completed` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 9(8) first sentence the testing of the high-risk AI system is performed throughout development and in any event before placing on the market` MEANS
    CONSIDER `Arts 8 to 15 the gate for the requirement` `the date asked` `the AI system` `the harmonisation facts` (`Article reference` OF 9, "", 8)
    WHEN `Arts 8 to 15 gate the requirement applies` THEN
        JUST (`the testing is performed, as appropriate, at any time throughout the development process` AND (`the date on which the testing of the high-risk AI system was completed` LESS THAN (`the AI system`'s `date placed on the market or put into service`)))  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "shall be performed, as appropriate, at any time throughout the development process, and, in any event, prior to their being placed on the market or put into service"
    WHEN `Arts 8 to 15 gate cut off by Article 2(2)` THEN JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): Article 2(2) "only Article 6(1), Article 60a and Articles 102 to 112 shall apply" to a high-risk AI system under Article 6(1) related to Section B products (seam S14, the keel's answer)
    WHEN `Arts 8 to 15 gate may be limited under Article 2(13)` THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): Article 2(13) says the application of this requirement "may be limited"; how far is for the delegated acts it names
    OTHERWISE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): Chapter III Section 2 applies from the date Article 113(c) gives, and Article 111(2) saves a system placed earlier and not significantly changed

